course: dictionary
lesson: 6859
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Overall is one of them. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning to use. «The overall cost» means the total cost of everything added together, so overall means total here.
explain: «Overall, it was a good day.» Here overall comes at the start of the sentence and means in general, taking everything into account. Some parts of the day may have been bad, but when you think about the whole day, it was good.
explain: Ask yourself: is this word adding everything up, or giving the big picture? If it sits before a noun like cost, score or winner, it usually means total. If it starts a sentence and sums things up, it means in general.
explain: Overall can also be a noun. An overall is a loose coat worn over clothes to keep them clean (UK). Overalls are trousers with a bib and straps, or a one-piece work suit. Watch the clues: the context tells you which kind of word it is.
fact: Overall (adjective) means including everything; total, as in «the overall cost».
fact: Overall (adverb) means in general, taking everything into account, as in «Overall, it was a good day».
fact: In maths, overall means the total or the whole result: overall score, overall winner.
fact: An overall (UK) is a loose coat worn over clothes to keep them clean.
fact: Overalls are trousers with a bib and straps, or a one-piece work suit.
exercise: «The school's overall total was 300 points.» What does overall mean here? | Lost in the woods | *Including everything; the total | Very old | Only just
exercise: «Overall, it was a good day, even with the rain.» What does overall mean here? | Very hungry | *In general, taking everything into account | Loud and noisy | Muddy and slippery
exercise: The art teacher says, «Put on your overalls before painting.» What are overalls? | *Trousers with a bib and straps, or a one-piece work suit | A bag for paints | A loose coat worn over clothes to keep them clean | A kind of paintbrush
test: «Betting companies set the odds so that, overall, they always make money.» What does overall mean in this sentence? | *In general, taking everything into account | Only just | Including everything; the total | Short and rude
test: Ella says, «The overall winner gets a gold medal.» Which meaning fits best? | *Total; the final result after everything is counted | Muddy and slippery | In general, taking everything into account | Giving out light
exam: Jayden says, «Overall, the match was close.» Which is the best meaning of overall here? | Lost in the woods | *In general, taking everything into account | Including everything; the total score | Very old
